# "last played" widget — Spotify Web API.
#
# If any of these are missing, the widget just doesn't render (no error,
# no placeholder). Safe to leave unset while developing everything else.

# 1. Create an app at https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard, add
#    http://127.0.0.1:3000/callback as a redirect URI, then copy its
#    Client ID and Client Secret.
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# 2. One-time only: run the authorization-code flow by hand to mint a
#    refresh token for your own account (scope: user-read-recently-played).
#      a. Visit, in a browser, replacing YOUR_CLIENT_ID:
#         https://accounts.spotify.com/authorize?client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID&response_type=code&redirect_uri=http://127.0.0.1:3000/callback&scope=user-read-recently-played
#      b. You'll be redirected to a URL with ?code=... — copy that code.
#      c. Exchange it for tokens:
#         curl -X POST https://accounts.spotify.com/api/token \
#           -H "Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded" \
#           -d grant_type=authorization_code \
#           -d code=THE_CODE_FROM_STEP_B \
#           -d redirect_uri=http://127.0.0.1:3000/callback \
#           -u YOUR_CLIENT_ID:YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET
#      d. Copy the "refresh_token" field from the response below.
#         It doesn't expire until you revoke the app's access.
SPOTIFY_REFRESH_TOKEN=
